# CLAUDE.md

Local instructions for coding agents on portfolio-app-new. `scripts/init.sh` creates this file from `scripts/templates/CLAUDE.md.template` when it is missing. It is listed in `.gitignore` and is not tracked in Git. `.sdd/constitution.md` takes precedence over this file.

## Read before planning or editing

- `.sdd/constitution.md` (governing rules, generated from `config.yaml`; never edit it by hand)
- `docs/PRODUCT.md` (approved discovery: use cases, requirements, stack, risks and roadmap; the decision source)
- `adr.md` (live architecture decision records)
- `config.yaml` (normalized configuration; every value and its source is in the Configuration Decisions table of `docs/PRODUCT.md`)
- `.sdd/SPEC.md`, `.sdd/PLAN.md` and `.sdd/TASKS.md` (requirements, Work Items and tasks)

## Rules that matter most

- Work follows `FR > WI > Task`. Do the next unchecked task in dependency order, and update `.sdd/TASKS.md` and `.sdd/CHANGELOG.md` in the same change.
- Commit subjects: `type(scope): imperative summary [FR-xxx][WI-xxx][TASK-xxx]`. Never bypass the hooks.
- Ask for approval before adding or upgrading a dependency, changing the database schema, or expanding scope beyond the requirements.
- An architecture change needs a `Proposed` ADR in `adr.md` that the user accepts before it is implemented.
- No rebase, amend of pushed commits or force-push without approval. After pushing, leave the working tree on the pushed PR branch and give the PR URL.
- Delivery: when the assigned task(s) are done and verified, create the branch `sdd/<WI>-<TASK-ids>` from `main`, commit with the traced subject, push, open the PR to `main` with `gh pr create`, leave the tree on that branch, give the PR URL and stop. Do not merge: the user and the reviewing agent review the PR. Several agents may work at once, so stay inside the assigned tasks and files, and commit only the files of your own task.
- `.env` is a dotenv file whose values may contain shell metacharacters. Never `source` it in a shell and never print its secrets; parse it as a dotenv file.
- Never commit secrets. `.env` stays local, and `KG_USER` must be a read-only GraphDB user.
